VALUES (1, 'openai-compatible', 'https://api.openai.com/v1', '', 'gpt-4o-mini', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE provider=provider;




-- Easy (6)
('The Tortoise and the Hare',
 'A classic fable about a slow tortoise who wins a race against a fast but overconfident hare. Learn vocabulary about speed, pride, and perseverance.',
 'A hare lived in a forest. He was very fast. He laughed at a tortoise who walked slowly. The tortoise said "Let us have a race." The hare said "This will be easy." The race began. The hare ran very fast. He looked back and could not see the tortoise. He felt tired. He decided to rest under a tree. "I am so far ahead," he said. "I can sleep for a while." He fell asleep. The tortoise kept walking slowly. Step by step, he passed the sleeping hare. When the hare woke up, he saw the tortoise near the finish line. He ran fast but it was too late. The tortoise won. The moral of the story is slow and steady wins the race.',
 'Classic Fables', 'easy', 'story,perseverance,pride', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Boy Who Cried Wolf',
 'A short story about a shepherd boy who learns that lying makes people stop trusting you. Focus words: shepherd, bored, villagers, trust, liar.',
 'A young boy watched sheep for his village. Every day he sat on a hill. He felt very bored. One day he shouted "Wolf Wolf help A wolf is eating the sheep" The villagers ran up the hill with sticks. They saw no wolf. The boy laughed. The villagers were not happy. A few days later the boy shouted again "Wolf Wolf" The villagers ran up again. There was no wolf. They were very angry. Then one day a real wolf came. The boy shouted "Wolf Wolf Please help me" The villagers heard him. They said "He is joking again." Nobody came. The wolf ate the sheep. The boy learned a hard lesson. Nobody believes a liar even when they tell the truth.',
 'Classic Fables', 'easy', 'story,honesty,trust', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Sun and the Wind',
 'A fable about the sun and the wind arguing about who is stronger. Teaches that kindness is more powerful than force. Key words: argue, shine, blow, coat, gentle.',
 'The Sun and the Wind had an argument. The Wind said "I am stronger than you." The Sun said "No I am stronger." They saw a man walking on the road. He wore a warm coat. The Wind said "I can take his coat off. Watch me." The Wind blew hard. It blew and blew. But the man held his coat tighter. The Wind could not take it off. Then the Sun tried. It shone gently. It gave warm light. The man felt warm. He smiled. He took off his coat. The Sun said "See Kindness is stronger than force. Gentle warmth can do what rough wind cannot do."',
 'Classic Fables', 'easy', 'story,kindness,strength', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Ant and the Grasshopper',
 'A story about an ant who works hard all summer while a grasshopper plays. Teaches the value of preparation. Key words: ant, grasshopper, prepare, store, winter.',
 'It was summer. The sun was warm. A grasshopper sat in the sun. He sang and played all day. An ant walked by. She carried a piece of food. The grasshopper said "Come and play with me Summer is long and fun." The ant said "I am storing food for winter. You should do the same." The grasshopper laughed. "Winter is far away," he said. He continued to play. Summer ended. Winter came. The grasshopper had no food. He was cold and hungry. He went to the ant. "Please give me some food," he said. The ant said "I worked while you played. But I will share with you this time. Remember to prepare next year."',
 'Classic Fables', 'easy', 'story,preparation,hard-work', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Lion and the Mouse',
 'A gentle story about a tiny mouse who saves a mighty lion. Shows that even small friends can help in big ways. Key words: lion, mouse, spare, net, chew, grateful.',
 'A lion was sleeping in the forest. A little mouse ran across his face. The lion woke up. He was angry. He caught the mouse with his big paw. The mouse said "Please let me go I can help you one day." The lion laughed. "You are so small. How can you help me" But the lion let the mouse go. A few days later the lion walked into a hunter''s net. He could not move. He roared loudly. The mouse heard the roar. He ran to the lion. He used his sharp teeth to chew the rope. He chewed and chewed until the lion was free. The lion said "Thank you little friend. You are small but you saved my life."',
 'Classic Fables', 'easy', 'story,kindness,gratitude', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Fox and the Grapes',
 'A fable about a fox who cannot reach some grapes and decides they are sour. Teaches about accepting disappointment. Key words: fox, grapes, vine, reach, sour.',
 'A fox walked through a garden. He saw big purple grapes hanging from a high vine. The grapes looked sweet and delicious. The fox wanted to eat them. He stood on his back legs and jumped. But the grapes were too high. He tried again and again. He jumped higher each time. He could not reach them. He stepped back and looked at the grapes. He felt frustrated. Then he said "Those grapes are probably sour. They are not good to eat anyway." He walked away with his head high. Sometimes people pretend to hate what they cannot have. But it is okay to simply accept disappointment and move on.',
 'Classic Fables', 'easy', 'story,pride,acceptance', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),

-- Medium (6)
('The Oak and the Reed',
 'A thoughtful story about a strong oak tree and a thin reed. Teaches that flexibility and humility are sometimes stronger than pride. Key words: oak, reed, bend, storm, humble.',
 'A tall oak tree stood beside a river. It was proud of its strength. Next to it grew a thin reed. The reed bent in the wind. The oak said "Look at me. I am strong and straight. The wind cannot move me. But you bend and bow to every breeze. It is shameful." The reed said quietly "I am not strong like you. But I survive because I bend." One night a great storm came. The wind was fierce. The oak stood tall and fought the wind with all its strength. The reed bent low to the ground. The wind grew stronger. The oak could not resist anymore. With a loud crack it fell into the river. When the storm passed the reed stood up again unharmed. Flexibility can be stronger than pride.',
 'Classic Fables', 'medium', 'story,flexibility,humility', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Two Friends and the Bear',
 'A well known story about two friends who meet a bear in the forest. It explores what true friendship really means. Key words: bear, pretend, danger, loyal, abandon.',
 'Two friends were walking through a dark forest. They promised to stay together no matter what. Suddenly a large bear appeared. It made a loud sound. One friend immediately climbed a tall tree. He hid among the branches. The other friend could not climb trees. He had to think fast. He lay down on the ground. He held his breath and pretended to be dead. The bear came closer. It sniffed the boy''s ear. It sniffed his body. The bear thought he was dead. Bears do not touch dead bodies. The bear walked away. The friend in the tree came down. He asked "What did the bear whisper in your ear" The other friend said "The bear told me not to travel with someone who abandons me when danger comes." A true friend stays by your side in difficult times.',
 'Classic Fables', 'medium', 'story,friendship,loyalty', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Greedy Dog',
 'A story about a dog who loses everything because he wants more than he has. Teaches about greed and contentment. Key words: greedy, bone, reflection, lose, content.',
 'A dog found a large bone on a farm. He was very pleased with himself. He held the bone firmly in his mouth. He decided to take it home to eat it in peace. On the way home he crossed a narrow bridge over a river. He looked down into the water. He saw another dog looking up at him. That dog also had a bone in its mouth. The dog did not know he was looking at his own reflection. He thought the other dog''s bone looked bigger than his. He wanted that bone too. He growled at the dog in the water. The dog in the water growled back. He opened his mouth to bark. When he opened his mouth his own bone fell into the river. It sank to the bottom. He lost everything because he wanted more than he needed.',
 'Classic Fables', 'medium', 'story,greed,contentment', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Kind Stranger',
 'An inspiring story about a young woman who receives help from a stranger and later repays the kindness. Shows how one generous act can create a chain of good.',
 'A young woman walked along a dusty road. She was traveling to a new city where she hoped to find work. She had no money and no food left. She sat down under a tree. She felt hopeless. An old man passed by. He saw her sad face. He stopped and gave her bread and fresh water. She thanked him. He also gave her a small bag of coins. He said "One day you will help someone else. That is how kindness travels." Years passed. The woman became a doctor. She never forgot the old man. She searched for him and finally found him living alone in a small house. He was sick. She treated him for free. She stayed with him until he recovered. The old man cried tears of joy. His small kind act had grown into something beautiful.',
 'Classic Stories', 'medium', 'story,kindness,community', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Little Star That Found Its Place',
 'A gentle story about a small star who feels unimportant. Teaches that everyone has unique beauty and value. Key words: star, shine, bright, gentle, unique.',
 'In the wide night sky there lived a little star. She was very small. Every night she looked at the big bright stars around her. They shone with brilliant light. She tried to shine as brightly as they did. She pushed herself hard. But she could only give a soft gentle glow. She felt sad and useless. One night a little girl looked up at the sky. She saw the big stars. They were beautiful. But then she noticed one small star. It did not shine as bright as the others. It shone with a quiet steady light. The girl said "That little star is my favorite. It looks warm and kind." The little star heard this. She understood something important for the first time. Every star has its own kind of light. You do not need to be the brightest to be loved.',
 'Classic Stories', 'medium', 'story,confidence,uniqueness', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Wise Old Owl',
 'A thoughtful story about an owl who becomes wise by watching and listening. Teaches that wisdom comes from careful observation. Key words: owl, observe, listen, wisdom, silence.',
 'An old owl lived in a tall oak tree. She was known as the wisest creature in the forest. Animals came from far away to ask her questions. A young rabbit once asked "Why are you so wise" The owl said "I watch and I listen. That is my secret." She explained that every day she watched the animals from her branch. She noticed that happy animals spoke gently. Unhappy animals made noise. She saw that animals who showed off were often lonely. She observed that the busiest animals were not always the most productive. She said "Most creatures speak too much and listen too little. They miss the lessons around them." The rabbit asked "How can I become wise" The owl said "Spend one day in silence. Watch the world. Listen to what is not said. You will learn more than a thousand books can teach you."',
 'Classic Stories', 'medium', 'story,wisdom,observation', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),

-- Hard (6)
('The Empty Pot',
 'A Chinese folk tale about an honest boy who wins an emperor''s contest with an empty pot. A powerful story about the courage to be truthful. Key words: emperor, seed, honest, ashamed, integrity.',
 'Long ago an emperor of China loved flowers. He was growing old and needed to choose a successor. He gathered the children of the kingdom. He gave each child a seed and said "Plant this seed. In one year bring me the most beautiful flower you grow. The child who grows the most beautiful flower will become the next emperor." A boy named Ping took his seed home. He planted it carefully in a pot. He watered it every day. But nothing grew. Weeks passed. Months passed. Still nothing. He felt ashamed. The year passed. The day of the contest arrived. All the children brought beautiful pots with colorful flowers. When the emperor saw Ping with his empty pot he asked "Why did you bring an empty pot" Ping answered honestly "I planted your seed and cared for it every day but it would not grow." The emperor smiled. He announced that Ping would be the next emperor. He had boiled all the seeds before giving them to the children. Only Ping had been brave enough to be honest.',
 'World Tales', 'hard', 'story,honesty,courage,integrity', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Merchant and the Parrot',
 'A Persian story about a clever parrot who tricks a merchant into setting him free. A tale of wisdom and the universal desire for freedom. Key words: merchant, cage, message, freedom, clever.',
 'A wealthy merchant kept a parrot in a golden cage. The parrot could speak several languages. The merchant loved showing him off to visitors. One morning the merchant announced he would travel to India. The parrot said "Please deliver a message to the wild parrots in the Indian forest. Tell them that I live in a cage but I remember the sky." The merchant thought this was strange but he agreed. In India he found a group of wild parrots in a forest. He delivered the message. As soon as he spoke the words one parrot fell from its branch and lay still on the ground. The merchant felt sorry that his message had caused such sadness. He returned home. When he told his parrot what had happened the parrot immediately fell to the floor of his cage. He lay still. The merchant cried "My beloved parrot is dead" He opened the cage and picked up the parrot. In that moment the parrot flew out of his hands. He perched on the open window and said "The parrot in India taught me that I must pretend to die to be free. Thank you for bringing me to the window." He flew away into the sky.',
 'World Tales', 'hard', 'story,wisdom,freedom,clever', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Last Leaf',
 'A touching story adapted from O. Henry. A sick girl believes she will die when the last leaf falls from an old vine outside her window. A tale of hope sacrifice and the power of believing.',
 'Two young artists named Sue and Johnsy shared a small apartment. Johnsy became severely ill with pneumonia. The doctor said she needed hope more than medicine. Outside their window grew an old vine. Its leaves were falling one by one in the autumn wind. Johnsy began to count the leaves. She told Sue "When the last leaf falls I will die too." Sue tried to comfort her but Johnsy would not listen. There was an old artist named Behrman who lived downstairs. He had always dreamed of painting a masterpiece. Sue told him about Johnsy. That night a terrible storm raged. But in the morning one leaf still hung on the vine. Johnsy watched it all day. She said "If that leaf can hold on through the storm maybe I can too." She began to recover. Later Sue discovered the truth. The leaf had fallen during the storm. Behrman had painted a perfect leaf on the wall during the night. He caught pneumonia in the cold rain. He never woke up. He had painted his masterpiece.',
 'Classic Tales', 'hard', 'story,hope,sacrifice,perseverance', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Gardener''s Garden',
 'A story about an old gardener who patiently nurtures a single seed while others rush to plant new things. A meditation on patience dedication and the value of waiting. Key words: gardener, patience, seed, bloom, endure.',
 'An old gardener planted a single seed in the corner of his garden. He watered it every morning. He removed weeds. He talked to the soil. Week after week nothing appeared. His neighbor who owned the garden next door planted rows of vegetables. Within a month green shoots covered his garden. The neighbor said "Your seed was probably dead. Dig it up and plant something new." The gardener smiled and continued to water his patch of empty soil. After three weeks a tiny green shoot appeared. The gardener was overjoyed but did not celebrate too soon. The winter came. The neighbor''s vegetables died. The gardener covered his small plant and protected it from the cold. Spring arrived again. The plant grew taller. Three years passed. The gardener''s plant became a magnificent tree with branches full of beautiful white flowers. People came from other villages to admire it. The neighbor looked at his own garden full of ordinary vegetables. He said "How did your tree grow so strong" The gardener said "I gave it time. Many things that are worth having cannot be rushed. A garden planted with patience blooms forever.',
 'Classic Tales', 'hard', 'story,patience,dedication,endurance', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Mirror of Truth',
 'A reflective story about a magical mirror that shows a person''s true inner self. A journey of self discovery and personal growth. Key words: mirror, reflection, anger, kindness, transformation.',
 'In a small village surrounded by mountains there stood an ancient mirror. The villagers believed it was magical. They said it did not show your face. It showed your heart. A young man named Ravi heard about the mirror. He considered himself a good person but he often felt angry. His anger showed in small ways. He complained about the weather. He blamed others for his mistakes. He spoke sharply to his mother. He went to see the mirror. When he looked into it he saw a twisted angry face staring back. He was shocked. He said "This cannot be me." The old keeper of the mirror said "It is not your face. It is your spirit. The mirror shows who you have become. If you do not like what you see you have the power to change it." Ravi decided to transform himself. He started each day by saying one kind word to his mother. He helped his neighbors. He stopped complaining. After a year he returned to the mirror. When he looked he saw a calm peaceful face. The mirror was never magical. It was just polished silver. The change was inside him all along.',
 'Classic Tales', 'hard', 'story,self-reflection,truth,growth', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
('The Bridge Builder',
 'A moving story about an old man who builds a bridge across a river knowing he will not live to use it himself. A story about leaving a legacy for future generations. Key words: bridge, legacy, generous, generational, sacrifice.',
 'An old man named Thomas lived beside a wide river that separated his village from the nearest town. Every week people crossed the dangerous river by boat. Many had drowned. Thomas decided to build a bridge. His family said "You are seventy years old. By the time you finish you will be too old to cross it. Why waste your remaining years" Thomas said "I am not building it for myself." He carried stones from the mountain every morning. He mixed cement with his own hands. His back ached. His hands became rough and cracked. The village children laughed at him. They called him the foolish old man. But Thomas did not stop. After four years the bridge stood complete. It was strong and beautiful. For the first time people crossed the river safely. They gathered to thank Thomas. A little girl asked "Grandpa why did you build this bridge if you will not use it" Thomas knelt down and said "Someone built the road that brought me to this village. Someone planted the tree that gives me shade. We all stand on the shoulders of those who came before us. A bridge is not for the builder. It is for everyone who comes after. One day when you grow up you will build something for the next generation too. That is how we move forward together."',
 'Classic Tales', 'hard', 'story,legacy,generosity,sacrifice', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);

 'English essays are evaluated by grammar accuracy, vocabulary range, structure, and logic. A strong essay keeps the original meaning clear, uses examples as evidence, and connects ideas with suitable transition words.',
 CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
